From: zolotvok <zolotvok@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH 0002] Core: compile volatile-metadata-covered blocks with no listed access without TSO

Base: FEX-2610-101-g1c4f04b + 0001 (local commit 5648a1439). Not committed; applies with `git apply` (-p1).

ContextImpl::GenerateIR applies volatile metadata to a block only when the block lies in a valid range AND at least
one listed volatile access falls inside it. A block inside a valid range with no listed access gets
ForceTSOMode::NoOverride, i.e. the global TSOEnabled setting (ldapr/stlr for every load and store). That contradicts
what the metadata says (the compiler declared every volatile access in the range, and this block has none) and what
ExtendedVolatileMetadata documents ("Disable TSO for a full module: just provide the module name"): with only a module
name, every block without a PE-listed access kept TSO.

Measured impact (Witcher 3 on an Android phone with a Mali GPU, FEX ARM64EC under Proton): a vertex interleave loop at
witcher3.exe+0x1e447c0, inside a PE valid range and with 0 of 30 589 listed accesses, stored into uncached
HOST_COHERENT memory with stlr: ~1 520 ns per 40-B element (plain stores: 2.2-2.8 ns), ~20 ms per frame, 50 % of the
render thread. Forcing the blocks covered through ExtendedVolatileMetadata cut the render thread from 88.3 to 58.0
Mcycles/frame.

Change: such blocks get ForceTSOMode::ForceDisabled, except instructions the frontend flags FLAG_FORCE_TSO (mono hacks),
which keep ForceEnabled. Blocks with a listed access and blocks outside every valid range compile exactly as before.
New config VolatileMetadataCovered (bool, default true, AffectsCodeGen so the disk cache keeps the two codegens in
separate buckets); FEX_VOLATILEMETADATACOVERED=0 restores the upstream behaviour.

Local Blobferry/DroidDeck patch, not for upstream submission (FEX does not accept AI-generated code, see AGENTS.md).

SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
Written with AI coding agents, directed and tested by zolotvok: Claude Opus 5.5 (keeper), Claude Sonnet 5.5,
Gemini 3.8 Flash, Gemini 4 Argon (reviews)
---
diff --git a/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Config/Config.json.in b/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Config/Config.json.in
index dffc65632..f7f4e1420 100644
--- a/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Config/Config.json.in
+++ b/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Config/Config.json.in
@@ -660,6 +660,16 @@
           "When metadata is unavailable falls back to the currently enabled TSO options."
         ]
       },
+      "VolatileMetadataCovered": {
+        "Type": "bool",
+        "Default": "true",
+        "AffectsCodeGen": "true",
+        "Desc": [
+          "Code inside a volatile metadata valid range (PE metadata or ExtendedVolatileMetadata) that has no listed",
+          "volatile access is compiled without TSO, as the metadata declares.",
+          "When disabled, such blocks keep the global TSO options (the upstream behaviour)."
+        ]
+      },
       "X87ReducedPrecision": {
         "Type": "bool",
         "Default": "false",
diff --git a/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Context/Context.h b/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Context/Context.h
index 02198afd3..a26a6184b 100644
--- a/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Context/Context.h
+++ b/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Context/Context.h
@@ -377,6 +377,7 @@ public:
     FEX_CONFIG_OPT(SoftwareRNG, SOFTWARERNG);
     FEX_CONFIG_OPT(StrictInProcessSplitLocks, STRICTINPROCESSSPLITLOCKS);
     FEX_CONFIG_OPT(MonoHacks, MONOHACKS);
+    FEX_CONFIG_OPT(VolatileMetadataCovered, VOLATILEMETADATACOVERED);
     FEX_CONFIG_OPT(JITFeatures, JITFEATURES);
   } Config;
 
diff --git a/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/Core.cpp b/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/Core.cpp
index e07a7da1b..1892fab41 100644
--- a/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/Core.cpp
+++ b/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/Core.cpp
@@ -581,11 +581,15 @@ ContextImpl::GenerateIR(FEXCore::Core::InternalThreadState* Thread, uint64_t Gue
 #endif
 
       bool BlockInForceTSOValidRange = false;
+      bool BlockVolatileCoveredNoAccess = false;
       auto InstForceTSOIt = ForceTSOInstructions.end();
       if (ForceTSOValidRanges.Contains({Block.Entry, Block.Entry + Block.Size})) {
         if (auto It = ForceTSOInstructions.lower_bound(Block.Entry); It != ForceTSOInstructions.end() && *It < Block.Entry + Block.Size) {
           InstForceTSOIt = It;
           BlockInForceTSOValidRange = true;
+        } else if (Config.VolatileMetadataCovered) {
+          // The metadata covers this block and lists no volatile access in it: nothing in it needs TSO.
+          BlockVolatileCoveredNoAccess = true;
         }
       }
 
@@ -687,6 +691,8 @@ ContextImpl::GenerateIR(FEXCore::Core::InternalThreadState* Thread, uint64_t Gue
             }
           } else if (DecodedInfo->Flags & X86Tables::DecodeFlags::FLAG_FORCE_TSO) {
             ForceTSO = IR::ForceTSOMode::ForceEnabled;
+          } else if (BlockVolatileCoveredNoAccess) {
+            ForceTSO = IR::ForceTSOMode::ForceDisabled;
           }
 
           Thread->OpDispatcher->SetForceTSO(ForceTSO);
